From f1c99623b2fe0fa1c73c9e129e1cdf648c7764bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): stuck warning names clock-held deadlines and
 stays quiet when every ready card waits on one [daveey]

hermes-hub 2026-11-01 23:48Z: 43 ready cards waited on a Codex quota wall with a typed reset
(1793774148) and the dispatcher logged 'stuck ... subscription_quota_reset=43' every 5 min
with no deadline. A card held until a known deadline is waiting, not stuck.

- DispatchResult.clock_held / lane_candidates: guarded cards whose hold ends on a known clock
  (subscription_quota_reset receipt, rate_limit/infrastructure/owner_restart cooldowns).
- describe_suppression appends '(until <iso>[..<iso>])' to those reasons.
- all_clock_held(): the gateway dispatcher and the CLI daemon don't count a tick as stuck when
  every lane candidate of every ticked board waits on a known clock.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_stuck_clock_holds.py (warning content, no-fire and
fire cases on both the gateway watcher and the CLI daemon entry paths).
